1
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:26,960
<i>It's been three years since I last saw Ellen.</i>

2
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:30,670
<i>I've visited the Vankreift</i>
<i>family numerous times.</i>

3
00:00:32,210 --> 00:00:33,250
<i>However...</i>

4
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:36,290
Your Highness.

5
00:00:36,380 --> 00:00:39,830
Although you've come all this way,
I regret to inform you

6
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:43,290
that Lady Ellen is not here again today.

7
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:45,380
I see.

8
00:00:46,170 --> 00:00:48,920
<i>Not once have I been able to see her.</i>

9
00:00:49,210 --> 00:00:53,290
Please, come inside.
Would you like something to drink?

10
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:54,580
Thank you.

11
00:00:54,670 --> 00:00:56,790
Now, now, right this way.

12
00:00:58,710 --> 00:01:03,500
<i>Recently, Roren has started</i>
<i>welcoming us into the mansion.</i>

13
00:01:04,830 --> 00:01:10,290
<i>He must be feeling guilty</i>
<i>for disappointing us every time.</i>

14
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:17,540
<i>It's also... probably to convince us</i>
<i>that Ellen really isn't here.</i>

15
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:25,790
This tea is always so delicious.

16
00:01:28,290 --> 00:01:30,250
<i>I wonder when we'll ever meet...</i>

17
00:01:31,290 --> 00:01:32,960
Who are you guys?

18
00:01:35,830 --> 00:01:36,880
And you are?

19
00:01:37,250 --> 00:01:41,250
The daughter of Sauvel Vankreift,
the lord of this estate.

20
00:01:41,540 --> 00:01:43,250
So, who are you guys?

21
00:01:43,540 --> 00:01:45,960
Did Roren not tell you?

22
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:47,830
Of course not!

23
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:51,880
Gramps doesn't tell me or my mother anything.

24
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:53,670
Now, why are you here?

25
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:58,040
We came to see Ellen.

26
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:00,130
Ellen again?

27
00:02:00,210 --> 00:02:02,630
Even I haven't seen her.

28
00:02:02,710 --> 00:02:04,880
What? Not even you have?

29
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:08,580
That's right! All everyone talks
about is Ellen this, Ellen that!

30
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:12,500
Why does everyone want to see her, anyway?

31
00:02:15,330 --> 00:02:18,460
I wanted to apologize in person.

32
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:20,330
Hmm...

33
00:02:22,170 --> 00:02:25,540
Wait, are you the one always bringing gifts?

34
00:02:25,630 --> 00:02:26,670
Huh?

35
00:02:27,330 --> 00:02:29,460
Then bring me some too!

36
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:34,500
Your Highnesses, would you care
for some more tea?

37
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:36,790
Hold it! Did you just say "Your Highnesses"?

38
00:02:37,130 --> 00:02:38,880
You guys are princes?!

39
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:42,830
Lady Rafilia, mind how
you speak to His Highness.

40
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:45,170
D-Don't laugh at me!

41
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:46,580
Yes, I'm sorry.

42
00:02:46,670 --> 00:02:48,670
My sincere apologies.

43
00:02:48,750 --> 00:02:50,920
No, I don't mind.

44
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:52,630
Rafilia.

45
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:57,920
The next time I come by,
I'll be sure to bring you something.

46
00:02:58,210 --> 00:02:59,710
Yay!

47
00:02:59,790 --> 00:03:03,130
Lady Rafilia, please mind your manners.

48
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:07,080
Roren, thank you for your
hospitality. I'll come again.

49
00:03:07,170 --> 00:03:08,210
Of course.

50
00:03:09,750 --> 00:03:12,330
The prince said he'd bring me something!

51
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:14,830
Lady Rafilia...

52
00:03:16,790 --> 00:03:18,960
How many times must I tell you?!

53
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:21,250
Ah, I'm sorry!

54
00:03:23,170 --> 00:03:25,540
Brother, you seem to be enjoying yourself.

55
00:03:25,630 --> 00:03:30,210
I am. No one's ever spoken
to me like that before.

56
00:03:30,290 --> 00:03:33,250
Wasn't she just being brash?

57
00:05:06,130 --> 00:05:10,080
THE CURSE OF THE MINES

58
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:16,170
You look cuter than ever today,
my little princess!

59
00:05:16,250 --> 00:05:18,880
You're rather dressed up.

60
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:21,750
I'm going to visit Uncle's mine
to greet everyone,

61
00:05:21,830 --> 00:05:24,540
so I thought I ought to be properly prepared.

62
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:30,210
My, my! I see even you
get nerves, sweet Ellen.

63
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,790
W-Well... it's just...

64
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:38,460
Princess, are you heading somewhere?

65
00:05:38,540 --> 00:05:40,130
Van!

66
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:42,330
Fluffy!

67
00:05:43,170 --> 00:05:47,580
Father and I are going out to assist Uncle.

68
00:05:48,670 --> 00:05:50,670
Are you all right, princess?

69
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:52,920
She's just nervous.

70
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,580
Then I shall accompany her!

71
00:05:55,670 --> 00:05:57,580
Van, you're not ready yet.

72
00:05:57,670 --> 00:05:59,250
You have to be able to humanize.

73
00:05:59,630 --> 00:06:00,710
You're right.

74
00:06:00,830 --> 00:06:02,670
All right, let's go, Ellen.

75
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:04,290
Yes, Father!

76
00:06:04,380 --> 00:06:05,420
Oh...

77
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:07,420
We're off, Mother!

78
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:09,880
I'll see you later.

79
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:12,790
See you again, Van!

80
00:06:19,790 --> 00:06:23,380
<i>The princess hasn't played</i>
<i>with me at all lately.</i>

81
00:06:23,750 --> 00:06:26,790
<i>And here we've been doing it</i>
<i>since she was little...</i>

82
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,750
Van!

83
00:06:32,250 --> 00:06:33,880
Fwuffy!

84
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:37,210
Ah, Ellen, that's dangerous!

85
00:06:37,290 --> 00:06:40,330
Come now, why don't you
come back with Daddy?

86
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:41,830
No! Lemme go!

87
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:43,880
- No! Lemme go!
- What should we play?

88
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:47,460
Hmm, maybe it's too soon for hide and seek.

89
00:06:47,710 --> 00:06:48,750
Oh...

90
00:06:48,830 --> 00:06:49,960
Wha?!

91
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:52,080
Van!

92
00:06:52,330 --> 00:06:53,290
Huh?

93
00:06:53,380 --> 00:06:56,420
Van, what do ya wanna pway?

94
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:59,960
How about hide and seek, pwincess?

95
00:07:00,210 --> 00:07:02,580
She already knows the teleportation spell?

96
00:07:03,710 --> 00:07:08,250
Ellen! Where are you, Ellen?!

97
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:15,580
Cry.

98
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:19,460
Van!

99
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:21,460
Ellen!

100
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:24,250
Father, weggo of Van!

101
00:07:24,330 --> 00:07:26,040
Lord Rovel...

102
00:07:26,790 --> 00:07:30,960
What are you doing to my child?!

103
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:33,500
Didn't expect to lure you out too, Vint.

104
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:37,960
It's what I do to bring Ellen out of hiding.
Sorry for the fuss.

105
00:07:38,210 --> 00:07:41,250
I can't believe you'd do that to my child...

106
00:07:41,330 --> 00:07:43,670
- I don't care who you are!
- I wuv you!

107
00:07:43,750 --> 00:07:46,040
My bad. I said sorry.
Cut me some slack, will you?

108
00:07:46,130 --> 00:07:47,670
I wuv you!

109
00:07:48,750 --> 00:07:52,500
<i>Indeed, I must learn to humanize at once.</i>

110
00:07:54,630 --> 00:07:56,500
The princes visited again?

111
00:07:56,580 --> 00:07:57,540
Yes, Your Grace.

112
00:07:57,630 --> 00:08:01,460
However, I informed them of Lady Ellen's
absence and they returned home.

113
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:05,040
That's good. It is the truth, after all.

114
00:08:05,130 --> 00:08:11,790
Brother, the mine we're looking into today
originally produced a lot of silver.

115
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:14,790
However, it's seen a steep decline of late.

116
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:19,380
Because of that and other inevitable
circumstances, I've decided to close the mine.

117
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,250
That's what I intend to tell them.

118
00:08:22,630 --> 00:08:23,880
I see.

119
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:25,880
Now then, Ellen.

120
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:29,250
The mines are dangerous,
so stay with your father, okay?

121
00:08:29,330 --> 00:08:32,790
Not that I think he'd
let you run off on your own.

122
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:36,040
Of course not!
I'll be carrying her the whole time.

123
00:08:36,130 --> 00:08:37,750
What?

124
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:41,130
Your pawpaw wishes he could accompany you too!

125
00:08:41,210 --> 00:08:43,670
I'll bring back a souvenir, okay?

126
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:45,880
I shall be waiting!

127
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:49,330
By the way, is Grammie not here?

128
00:08:49,710 --> 00:08:54,170
That's correct. I didn't tell her
you'd be here today.

129
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:56,460
Huh? Why not?

130
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:59,250
Because she'd demand we
take her to the mines with us.

131
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:00,960
Most likely.

132
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:08,500
By the way, Brother, about those...

133
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,920
The ingots that Ellen created for us.

134
00:09:13,170 --> 00:09:15,080
Oh, those.

135
00:09:15,170 --> 00:09:18,380
I was thinking of just saying
they came from an old vault.

136
00:09:19,170 --> 00:09:21,750
If we say that they've been in the family,

137
00:09:21,830 --> 00:09:24,880
not even the royal family would bat an eye.

138
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:27,250
Good thinking.

139
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:30,040
Huh?

140
00:09:30,290 --> 00:09:33,250
There are too many carriages,
wouldn't you say?

141
00:09:33,330 --> 00:09:34,630
That's strange...

142
00:09:38,630 --> 00:09:42,170
You're far too green to try and outsmart me!

143
00:09:42,250 --> 00:09:44,830
Especially concerning the mine closure!

144
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:48,250
Grammie?! Are you coming with us too?

145
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:50,830
That's right, Ellen, dear!

146
00:09:56,130 --> 00:09:58,710
Alberto!

147
00:09:59,330 --> 00:10:01,460
I am terribly sorry, my lords!

148
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:05,040
I am so happy to be
on an outing with you, Ellen.

149
00:10:05,130 --> 00:10:07,580
It's like going on a picnic,
don't you think, Grammie?

150
00:10:07,670 --> 00:10:09,710
I know, right?

151
00:10:09,790 --> 00:10:12,170
It would appear Mother
is dead set on going...

152
00:10:12,250 --> 00:10:13,540
Yeah.

153
00:10:13,630 --> 00:10:14,920
Alberto.

154
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,040
We're counting on you.

155
00:10:17,130 --> 00:10:18,170
Yes, my lords.

156
00:10:18,790 --> 00:10:21,630
How dare you treat me like baggage.

157
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:28,170
I accompanied your father on inspections
before either of you were even born!

158
00:10:28,250 --> 00:10:29,960
You don't say.

159
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:31,460
My apologies.

160
00:10:31,790 --> 00:10:34,170
So that's why you're...

161
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:39,000
Grammie, I came in a dress.

162
00:10:39,580 --> 00:10:41,460
You'll be fine, Ellen, dear.

163
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:44,290
Rovel plans on carrying you
the <i>whole</i> time anyway, right?

164
00:10:44,380 --> 00:10:45,380
Of course!

165
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:47,460
Seriously?!

166
00:10:57,830 --> 00:11:00,750
Lord Rovel, Lord Sauvel! Welcome!

167
00:11:00,830 --> 00:11:02,880
Lord Rovel, it's been so long!

168
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:05,670
I heard you were coming with Lord Sauvel
today and couldn't wait to see you!

169
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:07,920
<i>I knew it. I feel so out of place.</i>

170
00:11:08,130 --> 00:11:13,170
<i>I've blown it.</i>
<i>What a terrible first impression.</i>

171
00:11:16,170 --> 00:11:18,080
My name is Ellen Vankreift.

172
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:21,250
I am Rovel Vankreift's daughter.

173
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:23,040
Goodness, Lord Rovel!

174
00:11:23,290 --> 00:11:25,630
Isn't she adorable?!

175
00:11:25,710 --> 00:11:27,170
Er, yes.

176
00:11:28,130 --> 00:11:32,580
I've brought my brother here today
to discuss the closure of the mine.

177
00:11:34,580 --> 00:11:37,420
So we really can't stay open, then...

178
00:11:41,170 --> 00:11:42,580
Everyone!

179
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:43,880
Milady?

180
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:45,000
Lady Isabella!

181
00:11:45,290 --> 00:11:46,670
It's been too long!

182
00:11:46,750 --> 00:11:48,920
My, familiar faces!

183
00:11:49,290 --> 00:11:53,460
You're about to talk business
with my sons, correct?

184
00:11:53,540 --> 00:11:54,630
Before that...

185
00:11:56,540 --> 00:11:59,920
I thought we might have some lunch,
so I came prepared.

186
00:12:00,330 --> 00:12:03,710
Ah, this reminds me of when
the late duke used to visit.

187
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:07,960
You're right! He used to bring
good food when he came too.

188
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:11,540
We always looked forward to it.

189
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,920
Father must've had his heart
stolen through his stomach.

190
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:15,960
For certain.

191
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:17,330
Yep, yep.

192
00:12:17,420 --> 00:12:18,460
Ellen, dear.

193
00:12:19,420 --> 00:12:22,960
You should know that food
is the best way to win people over.

194
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:25,170
Grammie!

195
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:29,080
Ah, that was delicious...

196
00:12:29,330 --> 00:12:31,540
Thank you so much, milady.

197
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:35,040
You boys still have healthy appetites!

198
00:12:35,330 --> 00:12:36,670
I'm glad to see it.

199
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:43,330
<i>They said this was originally</i>
<i>a silver mine, but...</i>

200
00:12:44,710 --> 00:12:47,540
<i>As I suspected, there's a lot of quartz here.</i>

201
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:49,500
Are you having fun?

202
00:12:49,880 --> 00:12:51,330
Oh, yes!

203
00:12:51,630 --> 00:12:53,960
I just love minerals.

204
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:55,670
Is that so?

205
00:12:55,750 --> 00:12:56,830
Yes!

206
00:12:58,500 --> 00:12:59,460
Oh...

207
00:12:59,540 --> 00:13:02,750
There's plenty,
so feel free to look all you want.

208
00:13:04,710 --> 00:13:06,750
Listen to this, Lady Isabella!

209
00:13:06,830 --> 00:13:10,540
Way back when, this guy
used to eat my share too!

210
00:13:10,630 --> 00:13:12,630
You know that's not true!

211
00:13:12,710 --> 00:13:14,750
Whaddaya mean it's not true?!

212
00:13:14,830 --> 00:13:17,290
I just ate what was leftover!

213
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:21,420
<i>I see. To everyone here, this place is...</i>

214
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:22,540
What's that supposed to mean?

215
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:24,580
<i>Oh, I know!</i>

216
00:13:25,420 --> 00:13:29,790
<i>If this mine is so rich in quartz,</i>
<i>it's bound to have silver over gold.</i>

217
00:13:31,250 --> 00:13:33,380
Atomic number 47...

218
00:13:35,380 --> 00:13:37,880
This white stone is so beautiful!

219
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,000
Huh?

220
00:13:39,330 --> 00:13:42,670
When you change the angle,
it's fun to see it sparkle!

221
00:13:42,750 --> 00:13:44,880
What? Did you just say it sparkles?

222
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,000
Yes!

223
00:13:50,880 --> 00:13:51,920
Don't tell me...

224
00:13:53,380 --> 00:13:57,080
Your Grace, may I please break
this stone and check inside?

225
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:58,460
S-Sure.

226
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:10,080
That's...

227
00:14:10,250 --> 00:14:11,500
What is it?

228
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:13,710
It's silver.

229
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:15,330
Silver? That's silver?

230
00:14:16,170 --> 00:14:17,460
It's silver, Your Grace!

231
00:14:18,750 --> 00:14:20,830
There may be more!

232
00:14:22,250 --> 00:14:23,710
W-Wait a minute!

233
00:14:24,210 --> 00:14:26,420
We can keep mining in these mountains!

234
00:14:28,540 --> 00:14:29,580
Huh?

235
00:14:34,250 --> 00:14:35,750
<i>Ellen...</i>

236
00:14:36,630 --> 00:14:37,750
<i>Yikes.</i>

237
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:40,710
Your Grace! There's no need to close down!

238
00:14:40,790 --> 00:14:41,790
We can stillâ€”

239
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:43,040
I said to wait!

240
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:47,540
Have you men already forgotten?

241
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:53,750
These mines are cursed by the spirits
because we've mined too much silver!

242
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:55,630
Cursed?

243
00:14:55,710 --> 00:14:57,670
So it's time...

244
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:07,750
<i>So that's what's going on.</i>

245
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:11,170
Father, Uncle Sauvel.

246
00:15:12,710 --> 00:15:16,460
May I speak with the men for just a bit?

247
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:21,000
My knowledge may be able
to help them in some way.

248
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:24,500
All right.

249
00:15:26,460 --> 00:15:30,880
Everyone, does the curse happen to involve
people coming down with symptoms

250
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:35,880
such as shortness of breath, coughing,
and phlegm, possibly fatal in some cases?

251
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:37,210
How did you know?

252
00:15:37,290 --> 00:15:40,380
Your curse... I have a feeling
I may know the cause of it.

253
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:42,750
Huh? She does?

254
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:48,170
For many years, you've all been
breathing in fine minerals and dust here.

255
00:15:48,540 --> 00:15:51,380
That's had adverse effects on your bodies.

256
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:54,830
In other words,
this isn't the work of a spirit.

257
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:57,460
It a disease called pneumoconiosis.

258
00:15:57,540 --> 00:15:58,540
Pneumoconiosis?

259
00:15:58,630 --> 00:16:00,080
It's not a curse?

260
00:16:00,170 --> 00:16:01,880
- There's no curse?
- First I've heard of it.

261
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:03,420
A disease, you say?

262
00:16:05,750 --> 00:16:09,880
So, this "pneumoconiosis"... Is it curable?

263
00:16:11,830 --> 00:16:16,380
I'm sorry. It's not possible
to rid you of it completely.

264
00:16:18,210 --> 00:16:23,880
That said, with time, we can get you
some relief little by little.

265
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:27,080
Is that true?

266
00:16:27,170 --> 00:16:32,500
If I could get the slightest relief from this
illness I've suffered from for so long...

267
00:16:33,420 --> 00:16:37,040
I would be grateful. Please, help us.

268
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:40,170
Ellen?

269
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:43,920
Father, let us first return to the mansion.

270
00:16:44,250 --> 00:16:47,380
I would like to discuss
something with you and Mother.

271
00:16:47,460 --> 00:16:48,670
Ori too?

272
00:16:48,750 --> 00:16:49,880
Yes.

273
00:16:52,790 --> 00:16:56,460
Everyone, please allow me some time.

274
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:58,540
I'll discuss this with my mother,

275
00:16:58,880 --> 00:17:01,830
and we're going to come up with a solution!

276
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:07,830
So, Ellen, can you truly treat this disease?

277
00:17:08,710 --> 00:17:10,130
In theory.

278
00:17:10,210 --> 00:17:11,250
In theory?

279
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:15,290
It's been too long since
the initial onset of their symptoms.

280
00:17:15,380 --> 00:17:19,540
Furthermore, when lung disease
yields complications,

281
00:17:19,630 --> 00:17:22,250
treatment becomes less certain.

282
00:17:22,330 --> 00:17:23,670
Complications?

283
00:17:24,130 --> 00:17:28,170
That's when the first disease
causes another to develop.

284
00:17:29,130 --> 00:17:32,250
You're knowledgeable
on many difficult subjects.

285
00:17:32,830 --> 00:17:37,750
What I know about the disease
is meaningless if I can't treat it.

286
00:17:37,830 --> 00:17:40,710
But you already told them you could.

287
00:17:41,330 --> 00:17:44,420
That's where I'd like to ask Mother for a favor.

288
00:17:44,710 --> 00:17:46,210
Me?

289
00:17:46,290 --> 00:17:50,790
Yes. I'm thinking of creating a medicine.

290
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:54,580
Wait! Can you really do something
like that, Ellen, dear?

291
00:17:55,330 --> 00:18:00,790
I'm thinking it may be possible
if I change the way I use my powers.

292
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:03,750
Yet I can't shake the feeling

293
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:08,210
that doing this may have
an impact on the human world.

294
00:18:08,830 --> 00:18:10,670
Ori, what do you think?

295
00:18:10,750 --> 00:18:15,380
Well, why not let Ellen do as she pleases?

296
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:16,420
Huh?

297
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:17,460
Come now!

298
00:18:17,540 --> 00:18:21,500
Yes, she may still be immature as a spirit.

299
00:18:22,080 --> 00:18:28,130
But she won't know how her powers affect
this world unless she tries, now will she?

300
00:18:28,210 --> 00:18:29,170
What?

301
00:18:29,250 --> 00:18:31,960
Ori! If something happens to Ellen, I...

302
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:33,960
Oh, it'll be fine.

303
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:37,210
If anything happens, we just won't
come back to the human world.

304
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:40,130
What?! No, that won't do! Absolutely not!

305
00:18:42,250 --> 00:18:45,460
Ellen, sweetie, this is your project.

306
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:48,630
You told everyone you could do it, didn't you?

307
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,540
So you should do it.

308
00:18:51,170 --> 00:18:52,250
Yes, ma'am!

309
00:18:52,330 --> 00:18:56,580
However, if you run into any problems,
you have to consult us.

310
00:18:56,670 --> 00:18:58,290
Don't ever forget.

311
00:18:58,630 --> 00:19:03,830
You've got me, your father,your grammie,
and your uncle to rely on.

312
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:07,460
Give it your all!

313
00:19:07,540 --> 00:19:09,580
I guess my hands are tied...

314
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:11,210
I'll do my best!

315
00:19:27,790 --> 00:19:32,630
Ori! Ellen's been holed up
for days and hasn't come out yet!

316
00:19:32,710 --> 00:19:34,830
You think she's all right?!

317
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:37,040
It seems she hasn't been eating much either.

318
00:19:37,130 --> 00:19:40,580
She probably hasn't even been sleeping!
No, I'm sure she hasn't!

319
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:45,170
She must be working really hard on that
medicine, so don't you go bothering her.

320
00:19:45,420 --> 00:19:46,880
But...!

321
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:51,460
She's fine. Let's have faith
and be patient, okay?

322
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:02,630
What's wrong, Van?

323
00:20:02,710 --> 00:20:05,080
She said I'm not allowed in there either.

324
00:20:05,170 --> 00:20:07,750
You got locked out too, eh?

325
00:20:08,380 --> 00:20:13,250
Ellen always gets tunnel vision
when she immerses herself in something.

326
00:20:13,630 --> 00:20:15,040
That is true.

327
00:20:15,130 --> 00:20:20,710
<i>When she first discovered her spirit</i>
<i>power to manipulate the elements... </i>

328
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:28,380
Ah, Ellen!

329
00:20:28,460 --> 00:20:33,330
<i>She didn't yet know how</i>
<i>to use or control her ability.</i>

330
00:20:34,290 --> 00:20:37,630
<i>The princess has changed since then, but...</i>

331
00:20:37,710 --> 00:20:39,210
I can't take it anymore.

332
00:20:39,290 --> 00:20:43,920
Oh, but Ori said not to...
Still, I'm worried!

333
00:20:44,250 --> 00:20:46,380
But if I open the door, Ori will...

334
00:20:46,460 --> 00:20:49,540
Ah, I'm worried! I'm so worried!

335
00:20:49,630 --> 00:20:51,670
Princess! Princess!

336
00:20:52,250 --> 00:20:54,290
Ah, that's it!

337
00:20:54,380 --> 00:20:55,830
Let me at it, Van!

338
00:20:55,920 --> 00:20:57,080
I can't take it anymore!

339
00:20:58,250 --> 00:20:59,380
Huh?

340
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:03,250
Oh, Ori placed a barrier, did she?!

341
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:06,710
In that case...

342
00:21:12,330 --> 00:21:14,580
<i>The various chemical formulas</i>

343
00:21:14,960 --> 00:21:18,290
<i>showing the structure of every</i>
<i>drug I knew in my past life!</i>

344
00:21:19,580 --> 00:21:22,290
<i>If I can write down as many</i>
<i>as I can remember, then... </i>

345
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:27,040
Ellen! Stop this right now!

346
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:53,170
Ellen!

347
00:21:54,290 --> 00:21:55,710
Princess!

348
00:21:55,790 --> 00:21:57,750
Are you all right, Ellen?!

349
00:21:58,210 --> 00:21:59,540
The medicine...

350
00:22:02,420 --> 00:22:03,960
It's done.

351
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:07,960
Ellen...

352
00:22:12,500 --> 00:22:14,420
You're burning up!

353
00:22:16,170 --> 00:22:18,330
To think you pushed yourself to this point...

